Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["\<\
Scalar annihilation into gravitons in \
Einstein\[Dash]scalar\[Dash]Gauss\[Dash]Bonnet theory\
\>", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"c172b2ac-429a-46cc-b0f8-03c067b40728"],

Cell["\<\
Tree-level p1 + p2 \[RightArrow] p3 + p4, with two incoming real scalars of \
mass m and two outgoing massless gravitons. The additional interaction is (g1 \
phi + g2 phi^2/2) times the Gauss\[Dash]Bonnet invariant. Both couplings are \
independent. Start in a fresh kernel and evaluate from top to bottom. This \
example follows the native FeynArts workflow of examples 09 and 10; it \
computes a polarisation-dependent amplitude, not a spin sum or cross section.\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ccd3dc1f-40f2-47b2-a4f3-9f672583368e"],

Cell["The minimal two-graviton scalar contact has been corrected. Both graviton Ward identities now vanish for the rebuilt model with symbolic D, mass and couplings. Start in a fresh kernel so FeynArts loads the corrected model. The checks below act on the tensor amplitude before inserting helicities. See Documentation/Verification/ScalarWardCorrection.md.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"c2f65a9f-1254-44ff-a87f-8502094214f9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

