Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Fix the on-shell kinematics and external polarisations", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bc07ce5f-6297-44c0-afd3-403ab8de68e4"],

Cell["\<\
p1 and p2 are incoming scalar momenta; p3 and p4 are outgoing graviton \
momenta. Thus p1 + p2 = p3 + p4 and s + t + u = 2 m^2. SetMandelstam receives \
all-incoming momenta. All tensors and scalar products retain symbolic D; no \
D -> 4 limit is taken. Generic physical scattering has s > 4 m^2.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"acd5ae5f-ca93-4730-a474-d9dffa549569"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"FCClearScalarProducts", "[", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SetMandelstam", "[", 
   RowBox[{
   "s", ",", " ", "t", ",", " ", "u", ",", " ", "p1", ",", " ", "p2", ",", 
    " ", 
    RowBox[{"-", "p3"}], ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"-", "p4"}], ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "m", ",", " ", "0", ",", 
    " ", "0"}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{4.001399975879428*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[7]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4c3fe538-0715-4ee2-81f3-da0c087c32c6"],

Cell["The following scalar products choose outgoing helicities H3 = 2 h3 and H4 = 2 h4, with h3,h4 = ±1, in a four-dimensional centre-of-mass external-state subspace. The argument -I selects conjugated outgoing polarisations; it is not a helicity label. The tensors and contractions retain symbolic D: these two helicities are not a complete D-dimensional polarisation sum. The chosen vectors are null and transverse, with the phases fixed by the scalar-product table below. A vector dotted with itself is different from its product with its complex conjugate.", "Text", ExpressionUUID->"8fdfb706-f455-4ff9-8013-1dad4845b99d"],

